      "impact": "Reduced decoupling and a lower voltage rating on the EPD power rail, which may cause unstable display operation or premature capacitor failure.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U5"],
      "pins": ["U5.13", "U5.14"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "SKW92A pins 13 and 14, named LAN_PORT3_TX+ and LAN_PORT3_TX- in the library part, are both tied directly to the GND net.",
      "expected": "These Ethernet PHY differential output pins should not be shorted to ground; they should be left unconnected or used for their intended Ethernet function.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX+\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"14\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX-\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the Ethernet PHY drives these pins, they will be shorted to ground, potentially causing excessive current, damage to the SKW92A module, or at least preventing the Ethernet port from functioning.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["C11"],
      "pins": ["C11.1", "C11.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(C11-Pad1)", "GND"],
      "observed": "C11 is a 0.1uF capacitor with pin 2 tied to GND and pin 1 left unconnected. Its footprint is an inductor footprint (Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder) despite being a capacitor part.",
      "expected": "A decoupling capacitor should have both terminals connected, typically between a supply rail and ground, and should use a capacitor footprint.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"59\") (name \"unconnected-(C11-Pad1)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"C11\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(footprint \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\")"}
      ],
      "impact": "C11 provides no decoupling or filtering because one terminal is floating; additionally, the wrong footprint may cause assembly problems.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Three anomalies were found: C1 has an incorrect value/rating versus the reference design, SKW92A Ethernet TX pins 13 and 14 are shorted to GND, and C11 is an open capacitor with an inductor footprint. These deviate from the intended design and would affect EPD power integrity, Ethernet PHY safety, and basic decoupling."
}

